	"title"		"More Network Capacity Renew by NgocDuy"
	"description"		"[h1]✨ WHAT'S NEW IN v4.3.44 (Traffic Light State Synchronization & Deadlock Prevention for Nodes 1..65K) ✨[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]Fixed Traffic Light State & Cycle Freeze (Vanilla & TM:PE Default Lights):[/b]
[list]
    [*] Fixed the persistent issue where traffic lights (both default vanilla and TM:PE default lights) never changed state, froze on green/red, or ignored cycles on nodes 1..65,535.
    [*] [b]Dual-Bank State Synchronization:[/b] Writes simultaneously to both [i]m_trafficLightState0[/i] and [i]m_trafficLightState1[/i], completely resolving the high-node bank inversion desync where game/visual renderers read the opposite bank (nodeId >= 32,768).
    [*] [b]Cycle Timeout & Deadlock Prevention:[/b] Enforces automatic phase cycling ([i]clock >= 3[/i]) so that lights cycle smoothly even when zero vehicles or pedestrians are queued on opposing red roads.
    [*] [b]Visual 3D Light Rendering:[/b] Accurately computes visual signal states using 7-bit shifted frame offsets for all 65,536 nodes.
[/list]
[*] [b]Strictly ZERO Direct Harmony Hooks into TM:PE Maintained:[/b]
[list]
    [*] All traffic light fixes strictly patch vanilla [i]RoadBaseAI[/i]. TM:PE Timed Traffic Light state is checked via lightweight [i]DynamicMethod[/i], cleanly yielding to TM:PE's simulation when active without any Harmony hook overhead.
[/list]
[*] [b]Expanded All TM:PE Simulation Arrays to 65,536:[/b]
[list]
    [*] Expanded [i]TrafficLightSimulations[/i], [i]customSegments_[/i], [i]PrioritySegments[/i], [i]JunctionRestrictions[/i], and [i]ParkingRestrictions[/i] to full 65,536 capacity.
    [*] Upper node stepping cadence calibrated to exact 128 nodes/frame (256 frames) and 512 TTL nodes/frame (64 frames) across full 65K range.
[/list]
[*] [b]Retains All v4.3.43 & v4.3.41 Protections:[/b]
[list]
    [*] TM:PE Save/Load deserialization crash immunization, comprehensive binary Payload v2 save/restore, and economy non-negative guards remain fully active.
[/list]
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]MORE NETWORK CAPACITY RENEW[/h1]
[b]The Definitive 64K Network Limit Breaker for Cities: Skylines[/b]
[i]Fully rewritten, optimized, and stabilized by NgocDuy[/i]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]WHAT IS THIS MOD?[/h1]
Have you ever hit the infamous [b]'Cannot create more objects of this type'[/b] limit while building your dream metropolis?
Vanilla Cities: Skylines caps your road and transit networks at ~32,000 nodes and segments.

[b]More Network Capacity Renew[/b] safely expands your game internal network limits to [b]65,536 (64K) Nodes and Segments[/b] - giving you double the building freedom!

Unlike unstable legacy experimental versions that caused fatal crashes and corrupted traffic, [b]Renew[/b] is engineered from the ground up for [b]maximum stability, accurate traffic simulation, and zero data loss.[/b]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]KEY ADVANTAGES & SUPERIOR FEATURES[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]64K Expanded Capacity:[/b] Doubles the maximum network node and segment limits (up to 65,536) and lanes up to 524,288. Build massive regional transit grids, hyper-detailed highway interchanges, and expansive subway networks without restriction.
[*] [b]Full Road & Building Placement Guarantee:[/b] Solved engine-level ToolController collision bitmask limits (65,536 bits), allowing smooth placement of roads, bridges, tunnels, intersections, and buildings without tool lockups.
[*] [b]Native Apple Silicon & Intel Mac Stability:[/b] Fixed deep engine crash loops, memory boundary overflows, and native crashes that plagued previous limit mods on macOS (M1/M2/M3/M4 & Intel) and Windows.
[*] [b]Complete TM:PE Compatibility:[/b]
[list]
    [*] Timed Traffic Lights (TTL) are 100% operational on expanded nodes (> 32,768).
    [*] Custom lane connections, lane arrows, speed limits, and priority rules are fully respected.
    [*] Node data and timed phases persist cleanly through save/load cycles without missing references.
[/list]
[*] [b]Accurate Traffic Flow & Real-Time Heatmaps:[/b] Full traffic flow color refresh across all extended segments without frozen vehicles or phantom deadlocks.
[*] [b]Safe Persistence Guarantee:[/b] Implements clean savegame serialization to ensure custom traffic setups and extended networks reload perfectly.
[*] [b]Deep Mod Ecosystem Compatibility:[/b] Seamless integration with Adaptive Roads, Network Skins, Node Controller Renewal, Move It, IMT, Network Multitool, Network Anarchy, Picker, Find It, etc.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]COMPATIBILITY[/h1]
Tested and fully compatible with the standard modern modding ecosystem:
[list]
[*] [b]Harmony 2.2+[/b] (Required dependency)
[*] [b]TM:PE (Traffic Manager: President Edition)[/b] (STABLE & LABS)
[*] [b]Network Anarchy[/b]
[*] [b]Adaptive Roads (ADR)[/b]
[*] [b]Network Skins 2[/b]
[*] [b]Node Controller Renewal[/b]
[*] [b]Intersection Marking Tool (IMT)[/b]
[*] [b]Network Multitool[/b]
[*] [b]Move It[/b]
[*] [b]Picker[/b]
[*] [b]Find It 2[/b]
[*] [b]81 Tiles 2[/b]
[*] [b]Advanced Road Tools[/b]
[*] [b]Improved Public Transport 2 & 3[/b]
[*] [b]Advanced Vehicle Options[/b]
[*] [b]More Vehicles Renew 2[/b]
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]REQUIREMENTS[/h1]
[list]
[*] [url=https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/?id=2040656402]Harmony 2.2.2-0 (CitiesHarmony)[/url]
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]BEST PRACTICES & RECOMMENDATIONS[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]Backup Your Saves:[/b] As with any mod altering foundational game limits, always keep regular backup copies of your favorite cities.
[*] [b]Persistent Saves:[/b] Once a city exceeds vanilla network limits (> 32,768 nodes/segments), this mod must remain enabled to load and manage those extended networks properly.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]
[i]Developed with precision and care for the Cities: Skylines community by NgocDuy.[/i]"
	"changenote"		"v4.3.44 - Traffic Light State Synchronization & Deadlock Armor for Nodes 1..65K: Fixed traffic lights state and cycle freeze on both vanilla and TM:PE default lights; implemented dual-bank state synchronization (writing to both m_trafficLightState0 and m_trafficLightState1 simultaneously) to eliminate bank inversion desync on high nodes (nodeId >= 32,768); added automatic cycle timeout (clock >= 3) to prevent traffic light freeze even with zero waiting vehicles; accurately aligned 3D visual light rendering with 7-bit shifted frame offset; expanded all TM:PE simulation arrays to 65,536; all implemented with strictly ZERO direct Harmony hooks into TM:PE."
